    "https://recrutement.psl.eu/o4vfz7amer": {
      "title": "Radiobiology Engineer (F/M) FLASH radiotherapy",
      "description": "Radiobiology Engineer (F/M) FLASH radiotherapy | PSL Paramètres d’accessibilité fermer Contrastes Défaut Renforcer Inverser Police (dyslexie) Défaut Adapter Interlignage Défaut Augmenter Justification Défaut Supprimer Aller au contenu principal fr ▼ fr en Menu RH Découvrir PSL Nos établissements La recherche à PSL La formation à PSL L’innovation à PSL Nos engagements La qualité au cœur de la stratégie RH Favoriser le développement des compétences Une université inclusive et sans discrimination Une université responsable et ouverte Index égalité professionnelle Formation Centre d'Innovation Pédagogique Ecole Interne Toutes nos offres Recrutement Primary tabs Voir Generate PDF Radiobiology Engineer (F/M) FLASH radiotherapy (F/H) Localisation du poste 91400, Orsay, France Télécharger en pdf Partager : Facebook Linked in Imprimer Postuler Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The Curie Institute Research Center France’s leading cancer research and treatment centre, Institut Curie unites a renowned research centre and a specialist hospital, fostering close collaboration between scientists, clinicians and healthcare professionals. It offers an environment of excellence where expertise comes together around shared values: care, humanity, openness, collaboration, efficiency, innovation, solidarity and commitment. Missions Activités principales Laboratory The ATOMIC team “Advanced Therapy in radiation Oncology and Molecular Imaging Characterization” (CNRS UMR9029/Inserm U1353/Université Versailles Saint-Quentin) develops new strategies to increase the therapeutic index of radiotherapy. The team brings together biologists, medical physicists and radiation oncologists. FLASH radiotherapy, discovered at Institut Curie ( Favaudon et al., Science Translational Medicine, 2014 ), delivers the dose in a fraction of a second. It reduces toxicity to healthy tissue while maintaining anti-tumour efficacy comparable to that of conventional radiotherapy: this is known as the “FLASH effect”. As part of the FRATHEA institutional project , Institut Curie is developing a new FLASH irradiator using very high-energy electrons (VHEE), designed to reach deep-seated tumours. You will conduct the preclinical studies needed to validate this equipment, working closely with the team’s physicists and radiation oncologists: a rare opportunity to take part, from the very beginning, in the development of an innovative radiotherapy technology. The position is based at Institut Curie’s Orsay site, at the heart of the Université Paris-Saclay campus, which brings together research teams in radiobiology and medical physics as well as the Institut Curie Proton Therapy Centre. Main responsibilities · Design and implementation of in vivo experiments : plan and carry out irradiation protocols in mouse models to assess the effects of FLASH radiotherapy, in compliance with regulations and animal welfare standards (3Rs principle); contribute to drafting project authorisation applications (APAFiS, the French ethics approval system). · Animal care and monitoring :), weighing, substance administration, anaesthesia, monitoring of clinical parameters. · Irradiation sessions : prepare, anaesthetise and position animals on the FLASH irradiator, in coordination with the physicists (dosimetry, scheduling of beam time). · Biological analyses : collect organs and samples; take part in analyses (histology, immunofluorescence, genotyping, flow cytometry) with other team members. · Data analysis and reporting : collect, organise and statistically analyse data; keep the electronic laboratory notebook; present results at team meetings and contribute to publications. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Education and skills -        Master’s degree (MSc) or engineering degree in biology, biotechnology, physiology or life sciences. -        Significant initial experience in vivo required (final-year internship, work-study programme or previous position); 2 or more years of professional experience is an advantage. -        Regulatory training in animal experimentation required: French “Applicator” certificate or equivalent (EU Function B); training in “Conceptor (EU Function C, project design) is an advantage and may be funded as part of the position. -        Proficiency in rodent handling techniques -        Knowledge of histology, immunofluorescence and molecular biology (PCR, genotyping); experience in flow cytometry is a plus. -        Basic skills in statistical analysis (GraphPad Prism, R or equivalent). -        Experience in radiobiology or in an irradiation environment is appreciated. Personal qualities -        Scientific rigour, observational skills and critical thinking -        Strong organisational skills and autonomy -        Ability to work in a multidisciplinary team (researchers, physicists, PhD students, clinicians) -        Good writing and communication skills; scientific English (reading articles, discussions in meetings). What we offer -        A pioneering project: the preclinical validation of a new FLASH radiotherapy technology. -        A multidisciplinary biology – physics – clinical environment, on one of Europe’s leading research campuses. -        Funded training (flow cytometry, statistical analysis, etc.). -        Recognition of your work, with co-authorship of publications according to your contribution. Contract information Contract type : Fixed-term contract (CDD) Start date: As soon as possible Contract duration : 12 months, renewable Working time : Full-time Remuneration : from 29240 € to à 33013€/year according to the current grids Benefits : Staff restaurant, 75% reimbursement of annual public transport pass, company health insurance Location : Institut Curie, Orsay site (Essonne, Île-de-France), Université Paris-Saclay campus – accessible by RER B Specific conditions : work in an animal facility and in a controlled area (ionising radiation); radiation protection training and dosimetric monitoring Contact To apply, please send your CV, a cover letter and the contact details of two referees Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis; the vacancy may close as soon as the position is filled. Publication date: 15/10/2026 Application deadline: 31 December 2026 Fidèle à l’héritage de sa fondatrice, l’Institut Curie est pleinement engagé en faveur de l’égalité professionnelle entre les femmes et les hommes. Convaincus que la diversité des profils et des parcours enrichit nos équipes et nourrit l’excellence de nos missions, nous invitons toutes et tous à postuler à nos offres. Nos opportunités sont ouvertes à des personnes en situation de handicap. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+5 Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact o4vfz7amer5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Type de contrat / de poste CDI Quotité de travail Référence o4vfz7amer Publié le 15/10/2026 Postuler Radiobiology Engineer (F/M) FLASH radiotherapy (F/H) Localisation du poste 91400, Orsay, France Établissement Institut Curie Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The Curie Institute Research Center France’s leading cancer research and treatment centre, Institut Curie unites a renowned research centre and a specialist hospital, fostering close collaboration between scientists, clinicians and healthcare professionals. It offers an environment of excellence where expertise comes together around shared values: care, humanity, openness, collaboration, efficiency, innovation, solidarity and commitment. Missions Activités principales Laboratory The ATOMIC team “Advanced Therapy in radiation Oncology and Molecular Imaging Characterization” (CNRS UMR9029/Inserm U1353/Université Versailles Saint-Quentin) develops new strategies to increase the therapeutic index of radiotherapy. The team brings together biologists, medical physicists and radiation oncologists. FLASH radiotherapy, discovered at Institut Curie ( Favaudon et al., Science Translational Medicine, 2014 ), delivers the dose in a fraction of a second. It reduces toxicity to healthy tissue while maintaining anti-tumour efficacy comparable to that of conventional radiotherapy: this is known as the “FLASH effect”. As part of the FRATHEA institutional project , Institut Curie is developing a new FLASH irradiator using very high-energy electrons (VHEE), designed to reach deep-seated tumours. You will conduct the preclinical studies needed to validate this equipment, working closely with the team’s physicists and radiation oncologists: a rare opportunity to take part, from the very beginning, in the development of an innovative radiotherapy technology. The position is based at Institut Curie’s Orsay site, at the heart of the Université Paris-Saclay campus, which brings together research teams in radiobiology and medical physics as well as the Institut Curie Proton Therapy Centre. Main responsibilities · Design and implementation of in vivo experiments : plan and carry out irradiation protocols in mouse models to assess the effects of FLASH radiotherapy, in compliance with regulations and animal welfare standards (3Rs principle); contribute to drafting project authorisation applications (APAFiS, the French ethics approval system). · Animal care and monitoring :), weighing, substance administration, anaesthesia, monitoring of clinical parameters. · Irradiation sessions : prepare, anaesthetise and position animals on the FLASH irradiator, in coordination with the physicists (dosimetry, scheduling of beam time). · Biological analyses : collect organs and samples; take part in analyses (histology, immunofluorescence, genotyping, flow cytometry) with other team members. · Data analysis and reporting : collect, organise and statistically analyse data; keep the electronic laboratory notebook; present results at team meetings and contribute to publications. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Education and skills -        Master’s degree (MSc) or engineering degree in biology, biotechnology, physiology or life sciences. -        Significant initial experience in vivo required (final-year internship, work-study programme or previous position); 2 or more years of professional experience is an advantage. -        Regulatory training in animal experimentation required: French “Applicator” certificate or equivalent (EU Function B); training in “Conceptor (EU Function C, project design) is an advantage and may be funded as part of the position. -        Proficiency in rodent handling techniques -        Knowledge of histology, immunofluorescence and molecular biology (PCR, genotyping); experience in flow cytometry is a plus. -        Basic skills in statistical analysis (GraphPad Prism, R or equivalent). -        Experience in radiobiology or in an irradiation environment is appreciated. Personal qualities -        Scientific rigour, observational skills and critical thinking -        Strong organisational skills and autonomy -        Ability to work in a multidisciplinary team (researchers, physicists, PhD students, clinicians) -        Good writing and communication skills; scientific English (reading articles, discussions in meetings). What we offer -        A pioneering project: the preclinical validation of a new FLASH radiotherapy technology. -        A multidisciplinary biology – physics – clinical environment, on one of Europe’s leading research campuses. -        Funded training (flow cytometry, statistical analysis, etc.). -        Recognition of your work, with co-authorship of publications according to your contribution. Contract information Contract type : Fixed-term contract (CDD) Start date: As soon as possible Contract duration : 12 months, renewable Working time : Full-time Remuneration : from 29240 € to à 33013€/year according to the current grids Benefits : Staff restaurant, 75% reimbursement of annual public transport pass, company health insurance Location : Institut Curie, Orsay site (Essonne, Île-de-France), Université Paris-Saclay campus – accessible by RER B Specific conditions : work in an animal facility and in a controlled area (ionising radiation); radiation protection training and dosimetric monitoring Contact To apply, please send your CV, a cover letter and the contact details of two referees Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis; the vacancy may close as soon as the position is filled. Publication date: 15/10/2026 Application deadline: 31 December 2026 Fidèle à l’héritage de sa fondatrice, l’Institut Curie est pleinement engagé en faveur de l’égalité professionnelle entre les femmes et les hommes. Convaincus que la diversité des profils et des parcours enrichit nos équipes et nourrit l’excellence de nos missions, nous invitons toutes et tous à postu